{"reference":"Revelation 22","book":"Revelation","chapter":22,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A Textual Variation at the Close","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"In Revelation 22:19, ancient textual traditions differ: some read “tree of life,” while others read “book of life.” The difference is worth noticing because the warning concerns losing one’s share in what the book describes; readers may therefore encounter either wording in translations or notes. The chapter’s tree imagery also includes leaves “for the healing of the nations,” and its closing combines revelatory vision, prophecy, and a message intended for circulation among churches.","verse_refs":["Revelation 22:19","Revelation 22:2","Revelation 22:6-21"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_revelation_022_8505937130684f38e79c54cd"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Images Carried into the Final Vision","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"The river and tree in the chapter’s opening belong to a larger pattern in which Revelation recomposes Ezekielian imagery—including throne, scroll, measuring, plague, battle, city, river, and tree—within its own literary sequence. This places the final vision within a sustained network of reused images rather than presenting its details as isolated symbols.","verse_refs":["Revelation 21:1-27"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_revelation_022_d1a5fcfed4a24251e4156b39"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"},{"id":"block_3","text":"The New Jerusalem vision brings together several images: city, bride, sanctuary, Eden, and renewed Zion. More broadly, Revelation repeatedly reworks Israel’s Scriptures, including Daniel, Ezekiel, Isaiah, Exodus, Zechariah, Genesis, and Psalms. The river and tree at the beginning of chapter 22 are therefore part of this layered portrayal of the city.","verse_refs":["Revelation 10:1-11","Revelation 11:1-19","Revelation 12:1-17","Revelation 13:1-18","Revelation 14:1-20","Revelation 15:1-8","Revelation 16:1-21","Revelation 17:1-18","Revelation 18:1-24","Revelation 19:1-21","Revelation 1:1-20","Revelation 20:1-15","Revelation 21:1-27","Revelation 21:9-27","Revelation 2:1-29","Revelation 3:1-22","Revelation 4:1-11","Revelation 5:1-14","Revelation 6:1-17","Revelation 7:1-17","Revelation 8:1-13","Revelation 9:1-21"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_revelation_022_52c1abcfb48cfb0dff7b2917"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}